  {
    "evidence_id": "MIG-FORD-EXPLORER-2020-20V788000-RECALL",
    "case_id": "MIG-FORD-EXPLORER-2020-20V788000",
    "title": "NHTSA Recall 20V788000 public disposition",
    "content": "Ford Motor Company (Ford) is recalling certain 2020-2021 Explorer and Lincoln Aviator vehicles.  The right hand motor mount fasteners may have been incorrectly tightened, and may loosen over time.\nWith a loose motor mount, motor vibration may cause the axle to disconnect from the engine and could result in loss of power, increasing the risk of a crash.\nFord will notify owners, and dealers will remove and replace the right hand motor mount fasteners, free of charge.  The recall began February 3, 2021.  Owners may contact Ford customer service at 1-866-436-7332.  Ford's number for this recall is 20S72.",
    "published_date": "2020-12-17",
    "source_kind": "public_recall_disposition",
    "citation_locator": "NHTSACampaignNumber=20V788000",
    "source_url": "https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/recallsByVehicle?make=Ford&model=Explorer&modelYear=2020",
    "is_close_material": true,
    "holdout_only": false,
    "is_demo_fixture": false,
    "retrieved_at": "2026-10-31T12:44:38+08:00",
    "saved_at": "2026-10-31T12:44:38+08:00",
    "raw_recall": {
      "Manufacturer": "Ford Motor Company",
